course: dictionary
lesson: 8085
title: Remarriage: marrying again
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a long word by looking at its parts. The start, re-, usually means again, as in rewrite and reheat. Marriage is a wedding and the married life that follows. Put them together and remarriage means getting married again.
explain: «Churches differ on same-sex marriage and on remarriage after divorce; these are disputed questions.» The sentence tells you that people do not all agree. Disputed means argued over. The clues are differ and disputed, which show that remarriage is a topic people hold different views about.
explain: A remarriage can follow a divorce, or it can follow the death of a husband or wife. Phrases such as «remarriage after divorce» and «a happy remarriage» show that the word is about what comes after a first marriage, not about the first wedding itself.
explain: A remarriage can bring a «blended family», where children from earlier marriages live together with step-parents and step-siblings. Those new family members are part of the wider story of remarriage, so the word is about family life as well as weddings.
fact: The prefix re- at the start of a word often means again.
fact: Remarriage means getting married again after a divorce or after a husband or wife has died.
fact: A remarriage is a second, or later, marriage.
fact: A «blended family» is a family made when parents with children from earlier marriages come together.
fact: Churches can teach different things about remarriage after divorce, so it is a question people discuss in RE lessons.
exercise: What does remarriage mean? | *Getting married again after a divorce or after a husband or wife has died | Living on your own for ever | Being a grandparent for the first time | Moving to a new house
exercise: «Churches differ on same-sex marriage and on remarriage after divorce; these are disputed questions.» What does disputed mean? | *Argued over, with people holding different views | Agreed by everyone | Very short and simple | Forgotten by everyone
exercise: In the same sentence, which word tells you that churches do not all agree? | marriage | *differ | churches | questions
test: A second marriage is another name for what? | A divorce | A wedding dress | *A remarriage | A blended family
test: What is a «blended family»? | A family that lives in a castle | *A family with children from earlier marriages living together with step-parents | A family that only eats together | A family with just one child
exam: Which sentence uses remarriage correctly? | The remarriage was the colour of the sky. | *Her remarriage took place two years after her divorce. | Remarriage is the name of a small green bird. | She ate a remarriage for breakfast.
